  "result": "The quiz is written: `quizzes/0002.json`, with its key in `keys/0002.json`. It has six questions on O4, titled \"Workflows and agents: who owns the control flow\".\n\n- **Heads-up:** O4 hasn't been taught yet, because there's no lesson on workflows versus agents. This quiz is ahead of the lessons, and I didn't write one.\n- **Who owns the control flow:** one multiple-choice question on what separates a workflow from an agent, and one short answer on a routing setup, where a model labels each message and code runs the matching steps.\n- **Cost and limits:** one question on why an agent usually costs more per request, and one on what a fixed workflow can't do unless its code changes.\n- **Applying it to the makerspace assistant:** picking which of four request types suits a fixed workflow under a small budget, and choosing which of two features to build as an agent and giving the reason.\n\nThe reviewer ran two passes, which is the cap, and I fixed what it found. The review record is in `review-records/0002-quiz.md`.\n\nThe key introduces misconception ids M7 to M10, which weren't in the workspace before. You can take the quiz whenever you're ready.",
